*; ============================================================*

*; THE BYZANTINE SHADOW*

*; MODULE 09 -- CAPITAL FEASIBILITY*

*; ============================================================*

*;*

*; PURPOSE*
*; -------*
*; Determine whether the active Module 08 production requirement*
*; can be financed while preserving the protected strategic reserve*
*; established by Module 07.*

*;*

*; ARCHITECTURE*
*; ------------*
*;*
*; MODULE 08*
*;   ENGINE-DERIVED REQUIREMENT VECTOR*
*;              |*
*;              v*
*;      up-get-cost-delta*
*;              |*
*;              v*
*;   GROSS CAPITAL SLACK*
*;              |*
*;              v*
*;   SUBTRACT PROTECTED RESERVE*
*;              |*
*;              v*
*;   RESERVE-ADJUSTED CAPITAL SLACK*
*;              |*
*;              v*
*;      FEASIBILITY STATE*
*;*
*; CAPITAL FEASIBILITY DOES NOT:*
*;   - change composition targets*
*;   - change production deficits*
*;   - change reserve policy*
*;   - modify escrow*
*;   - release escrow*
*;   - train units*
*;   - build infrastructure*
*;   - execute market trades*
*;   - authorize execution*
*;   - claim that a future income stream exists*
*;*
*; It answers one question only:*
*;*
*;   "Can the currently requested production package be funded*
*;    from the current stockpile without consuming the protected*
*;    strategic reserve?"*

*; ============================================================*

*; INITIALIZATION*
*; ============================================================*

(defrule
    (goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-INITIALIZED -1)
=>
    (set-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-INITIALIZED 1)
    (set-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-FOOD 0)
    (set-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-WOOD 0)
    (set-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-STONE 0)
    (set-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-GOLD 0)
    (set-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-FEASIBILITY SHADOW-CAPITAL-INSUFFICIENT)
    (set-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-ACTIVE SHADOW-CAPITAL-INACTIVE)
)

*; ============================================================*
*; CAPITAL SNAPSHOT*
*; ============================================================*

*;*
*; Module 08 owns the current four-resource cost vector:*
*;*
*;   SHADOW-PROD-COST-FOOD*
*;   SHADOW-PROD-COST-WOOD*
*;   SHADOW-PROD-COST-STONE*
*;   SHADOW-PROD-COST-GOLD*
*;*
*; These are 500-503.*
*;*
*; up-get-cost-delta returns:*
*;*
*;   current stockpile - current cost vector*
*;*
*; into four consecutive goals.*
*;*
*; Because the engine requires the cost-delta output to occupy*
*; extended goals in the 41-508 range, the calculation uses the*
*; existing 500-503 cost vector as the temporary engine output.*
*; The resulting values are immediately copied into the Module 09*
*; capital goals below.*
*;*
*; ============================================================*

(defrule
    (true)
=>
    (up-get-cost-delta SHADOW-PROD-COST-FOOD)
    (up-modify-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-FOOD g:= SHADOW-PROD-COST-FOOD)
    (up-modify-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-WOOD g:= SHADOW-PROD-COST-WOOD)
    (up-modify-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-STONE g:= SHADOW-PROD-COST-STONE)
    (up-modify-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-GOLD g:= SHADOW-PROD-COST-GOLD)
)

*; ============================================================*
*; RESERVE PROTECTION*
*; ============================================================*

*;*
*; The raw cost delta answers:*
*;*
*;   stockpile - production requirement*
*;*
*; Capital feasibility must answer the stricter question:*
*;*
*;   stockpile - production requirement - protected reserve*
*;*
*; Module 07's reserve goals are therefore subtracted here.*
*;*
*; The reserve goals are policy outputs, not escrow balances.*
*; This module deliberately does not touch escrow.*
*;*
*; ============================================================*

(defrule
    (true)
=>
    (up-modify-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-FOOD c:- SHADOW-RESERVE-FOOD)
    (up-modify-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-WOOD c:- SHADOW-RESERVE-WOOD)
    (up-modify-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-STONE c:- SHADOW-RESERVE-STONE)
    (up-modify-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-GOLD c:- SHADOW-RESERVE-GOLD)
)

*; ============================================================*
*; CAPITAL ACTIVITY*
*; ============================================================*

*;*
*; No production requirement means there is nothing to finance.*
*; Capital feasibility is therefore inactive when Module 08 has*
*; no positive deficit.*
*;*
*; ============================================================*

(defrule
    (true)
=>
    (set-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-ACTIVE SHADOW-CAPITAL-INACTIVE)
    (set-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-FEASIBILITY SHADOW-CAPITAL-INSUFFICIENT)
)

(defrule
    (goal SHADOW-REQ-ACTIVE SHADOW-REQ-ACTIVE-VALUE)
=>
    (set-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-ACTIVE SHADOW-CAPITAL-ACTIVE-VALUE)
)

*; ============================================================*
*; CAPITAL FEASIBILITY*
*; ============================================================*

*;*
*; Every protected resource must remain non-negative after paying*
*; the complete Module 08 requirement.*
*;*
*; This is intentionally conjunctive:*
*;*
*;   FOOD >= 0*
*;   AND WOOD >= 0*
*;   AND STONE >= 0*
*;   AND GOLD >= 0*
*;*
*; A surplus in one resource cannot compensate for a deficit in*
*; another. Market conversion is a later/subordinate decision.*
*;*
*; IMPORTANT: up-compare-goal takes exactly three arguments here:*
*;   goal, comparator, value.*
*; The literal zero is therefore written as 0, not c: 0.*
*;*
*; ============================================================*

(defrule
    (goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-ACTIVE SHADOW-CAPITAL-ACTIVE-VALUE)
    (up-compare-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-FOOD >= 0)
    (up-compare-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-WOOD >= 0)
    (up-compare-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-STONE >= 0)
    (up-compare-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-GOLD >= 0)
=>
    (set-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-FEASIBILITY SHADOW-CAPITAL-SUFFICIENT)
)

*; ============================================================*
*; EXPLICIT INSUFFICIENT STATE*
*; ============================================================*

*;*
*; This rule is intentionally explicit rather than relying on the*
*; initialization value. A capital deficit in ANY protected resource*
*; makes the current package infeasible.*
*;*
*; The engine/parser requires binary OR. The four-resource condition*
*; is therefore represented as a nested binary tree without changing*
*; the intended truth table:*
*;*
*;   FOOD deficit OR WOOD deficit OR STONE deficit OR GOLD deficit*
*;*
*; ============================================================*

(defrule
    (goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-ACTIVE SHADOW-CAPITAL-ACTIVE-VALUE)
    (or
        (or
            (up-compare-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-FOOD < 0)
            (up-compare-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-WOOD < 0)
        )
        (or
            (up-compare-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-STONE < 0)
            (up-compare-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-SLACK-GOLD < 0)
        )
    )
=>
    (set-goal SHADOW-CAPITAL-FEASIBILITY SHADOW-CAPITAL-INSUFFICIENT)
)

*; ============================================================*
*; END MODULE 09*
*; ============================================================*